{"id":"surface:range-habitat-white-tailed-ptarmigan-2.1.0","speciesId":"species:white-tailed-ptarmigan","metric":"HABITAT_SUITABILITY_IN_RANGE","unit":"habitat class inside the supported range","sitesSurveyed":110,"sitesDetected":110,"source":{"authority":"North Ground (range and habitat profile)","title":"White-tailed ptarmigan: habitat opportunity inside its range, methodology 2.1.0","url":"https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/search?taxon_key=5227717&country=ca&country=us&license=cc0_1_0&license=cc_by_4_0&hascoordinate=true&hasgeospatialissue=false&occurrencestatus=present&year=2000,2026&basisofrecord=human_observation&basisofrecord=preserved_specimen&basisofrecord=material_sample&basisofrecord=machine_observation&basisofrecord=observation","licence":"North Ground surface; inputs under CC BY 4.0 (Copernicus land cover), CC0 1.0 and CC BY 4.0 (occurrence records through GBIF.org) and the public domain (NOAA ETOPO 2022)","attribution":"Contains modified Copernicus Global Land Service information (2019). Buchhorn, M. et al., Copernicus Global Land Service: Land Cover 100m: collection 3: epoch 2019: Globe. Range from occurrence records published through GBIF.org (retrieved 2026-09-30) by the 15 datasets credited in content/intelligence/range-habitat/datasets.json. NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information. 2022: ETOPO 2022 15 Arc-Second Global Relief Model. doi:10.25921/fd45-gt74.","retrievedAt":"2026-09-30","verifiedAt":"2026-09-30"},"limitations":["How well the land suits white-tailed ptarmigan, inside the range records place it. Habitat, not a count of animals and not a density.","The range is ground within 20 km of places where openly licensed records confirm the species; where people rarely record wildlife, real range can be missing, and records can be wrong.","Records decide only whether ground is in the range; they never set a cell's colour, so where more people report wildlife does not become where there are more animals. Resident birds are recorded where birders and hunters go — farms, parks, roads — and released game-farm birds are recorded too, so a record can be a release rather than a population.","Unshaded ground is outside that range, rated unsuitable inside it, or open water, sea, ice or town the profile does not name as habitat. None of these is a finding that the species is absent.","Land cover is from 2019 and does not know forest age, recent fire or harvest.","Hunting geography and seasons play no part in this surface; the zone card says what is legal."],"observationPeriod":{"from":"2000-01-01","through":"2026-09-30"},"methodology":{"id":"methodology:north-ground-range-habitat","version":"2.1.0","effectiveFrom":"2026-09-30","history":[{"version":"1.0.0","detail":"First publication: range from clustered record squares, categorical habitat inside it."},{"version":"2.0.0","detail":"Ground inside the range rated unsuitable kept as its own state; water, sea, ice and town masked for profiles that do not name them; values placed on the grid nodes the renderer samples (1.0.0 sat half a cell south-west); an island rule for sedentary families; elevation and coast requirements; confidence from components rather than record counts alone. The concentrated-population rule (2 counted squares holding 300 records) was set AFTER the first 2.0.0 build declined kalij pheasant on 15,421 records in three squares of Hawaii Island: the five-square minimum was meant to refuse a handful of scattered reports, and refused a real island population instead. Recorded as set after seeing the result."},{"version":"2.1.0","detail":"Open water a profile names is drawn only within the profile's openWaterKm (else coastKm, else 5 km) of dry land, as the sea already was: under 2.0.0 mallard was painted across the middle of Lake Winnipeg. 'Water or wetland nearby' is a distance-weighted share falling to nothing at 20 km, replacing an unweighted 3 × 3 box that drew a hard-edged 0.3° square around every small lake (wild boar). Both set after seeing those surfaces. Gaps in the range no wider than the family's declared gapKm are joined by a morphological closing (grow by half the gap, shrink back), which can fill a hole between recorded places but never extend the range past its recorded edge or outside its convex hull; habitat and the masks still decide every joined cell. Set AFTER seeing the 2.0.0 alligator surface: 9,702 openly licensed records in 72 squares drew separate discs with central Florida blank — the records' sampling painted as absence. Recorded as set after seeing the result. And a correction, not a choice: each record square is now used at the size of the GBIF cell it stands for. The first reads' 0.35° squares were 1.40625° cells (GBIF aggregates 16 × 16 cells per map tile), so 2.0.0 drew ranges from a sixteenth of the ground the records covered, in bands with gaps between them."}]},"methodologyStatedAs":"Range: ground within 20 km of GBIF's 1.40625° cells holding 2+ openly licensed records since 2000, each within 150 km of another or holding 10+ on its own, with gaps of up to 60 km between recorded ground joined (110 squares, 11235 records). Habitat: each 0.1° cell's land cover read through this species' categorical profile (core 1, high 0.75, moderate 0.5, low 0.25, unsuitable 0), share-weighted, with required relationships as limiting factors; open water, sea, ice and town the profile does not name are masked. No weight is fitted.","scaleStatedAs":"White-tailed ptarmigan: habitat opportunity. Colour is the habitat class for this species inside its range — red core, orange and yellow strong, green moderate, blue marginal. Habitat, not a count of animals.","season":{"observedSeason":"All seasons (resident habitat)","matchesHuntingSeason":true,"warning":"Habitat is read from the land, which does not change with the season; where the animals are within it can."},"model":{"id":"model:north-ground-range-habitat-white-tailed-ptarmigan","version":"2.1.0","claim":"RANGE_HABITAT","inputs":[{"id":"foundation:landcover-cgls-lc100-2019-0.1deg","hash":"sha256:37891209b4ae816931a1f6a944c5ac2d2403c00f4cbfda71cacd710a050de525"},{"id":"open occurrence records (content/intelligence/range-habitat/inputs/white-tailed-ptarmigan.records.json)","hash":"sha256:fbfeadd01f9abc7784387a154b46e204780aa191ae92ec72b5e2b4cd5fe70bf9"},{"id":"foundation:terrain-etopo2022-0.1deg","hash":"sha256:676b594dbfa561b9ea7558fe4d537023d0e82042a0ee282051e9df53c7992d0f"}],"literature":["Rocky alpine tundra above timberline with low vegetation or damp alpine meadows near snowfields; in winter where willows extend above the snow. — North Ground's published profile of the species, citing National Audubon Society, White-tailed Ptarmigan | Audubon Field Guide; Colorado Virtual Library (Colorado State Library), Colorado's White-tailed Ptarmigan: Changing with the Seasons; NatureServe, Lagopus leucura (NatureServe Explorer)."],"reading":"Rocky alpine tundra and alpine meadow are core; willow shrub strong; snowfields moderate; open conifer marginal — and mountain relief is required, which keeps it above timberline.","profile":{"family":"RESIDENT_BIRD","reachKm":20,"landCover":{"CORE":["TUNDRA","BARE_SPARSE","HERBACEOUS"],"HIGH":["SHRUB"],"MODERATE":["SNOW_ICE"],"LOW":["NEEDLELEAF_OPEN"]},"edge":null,"requires":[{"feature":"RELIEF_METRES","thresholds":{"CORE":500,"HIGH":300,"MODERATE":150,"LOW":50}}],"coastKm":null,"season":null,"whyNotRangeHabitat":null},"range":{"confirmedSquares":115,"countedSquares":110,"islandSquares":4,"gapKm":60,"joinedCells":396,"recordGroup":"BIRD","edgeOnUnrecordedGround":0.049,"openRecords":11235,"datasets":15,"months":null},"cells":{"painted":15475,"unsuitable":12243,"masked":{"WATER":144,"SEA":1452,"BUILT":30},"noData":0},"variation":{"classShares":{"HIGH":0.273,"CORE":0.092,"MODERATE":0.365,"LOW":0.269},"usefulVariation":true},"confidenceComponents":[{"component":"range evidence","holds":true,"detail":"11235 records in 110 squares (needs 300 in 30)"},{"component":"habitat concordance","holds":true,"detail":"record squares on moderate-or-better land 35 in 100 against 34 in 100 across the range (ratio 1.04; needs 1)"},{"component":"seasonal applicability","holds":true,"detail":"all-year records for a species that stays"},{"component":"source age","holds":true,"detail":"records read 2026-09-30; land cover epoch 2019 (its age is reported with the surface)"},{"component":"resolution","holds":true,"detail":"habitat at 0.1° (about 11 km); range edge from 1.40625° record cells and 20 km beyond them"}]},"grid":{"latStep":0.1,"lonStep":0.1,"south":17.55,"west":-169.95,"rows":665,"cols":1200,"registration":"CELL_CENTRE_NODES"},"cellsEncoded":{"encoding":"U8_DEFLATE_BASE64","scale":4,"r0":175,"c0":136,"rows":299,"cols":526,"data":""}}
